= El ajusticiamiento

It arrives as a name whispered by three people who each heard it from the others: a compañero — young, nervous, present at two operations that went wrong — accused of being *oreja*, an ear for the enemy. The evidence is a pattern that is also the pattern of ordinary bad luck; the fear is real and it is not baseless, because the Colonel's map does keep filling and someone is filling it. The column has stopped meeting his eyes. They are waiting for a decision, and the decision is the oldest and worst the armed struggle ever forced on the people who chose it: *what do we do with the one we cannot trust and cannot prove?*

This is how the Liga ate itself. This is how every hunted movement learns that the enemy's deepest victory is not the informer he plants but the informers you invent to explain your losses. And it is also, sometimes, real. There is no clean hand at the end of this.

- @ajust_ejecutar: Authorize it. In a war this hunted, the doubt itself is a weapon the enemy is using; end it, and let the column see the leadership will not gamble their lives on a maybe.
- @ajust_investigar: Neither condemn nor clear — investigate. Hold him, pull the thread properly, accept the time and risk that a real informer stays operational while you do.
- @ajust_proteger: Refuse. The Movement does not shoot its own on suspicion; if it becomes that, it has already lost the thing it was for. Vouch for him, and carry the risk if you are wrong.

@ajust_ejecutar
go-to: post_event
on-arrival: ajusticiamientos += 1; paranoia -= 18; coronel_red -= 6; disciplina -= 6; moral_columnas -= 5; memorial += 1; sup_students -= 2; leyenda -= 1

It is done at dawn, away from the camp, by people who will not sleep well again. And the terrible thing — the thing that guarantees it will happen again — is that it *works*, in the only sense the fear can measure: the whispers stop, the paranoia drops, and for a while the losses ease enough to call it proof. Whether he was guilty no one will ever know, which is the point and the poison. The column obeyed and the column is smaller in a way that does not show on any roster: something went out of it at that dawn that no recruitment drive brings back. The name goes on your memorial too. You will not write down why.

@ajust_investigar
go-to: post_event
choose-if: inteligencia >= 20
unavailable-subtitle: A real investigation needs eyes and craft you do not have; without them, holding him only means the doubt festers under guard.
on-arrival: paranoia -= 8; inteligencia -= 4; disciplina += 2; expediente += 2

You do the hard, slow, unglamorous thing: hold him, and actually look — retrace the operations, test what he knew against what leaked, find the clerk or the courier or the coincidence that the fear had assigned to him. It costs you the intelligence effort you needed elsewhere and it costs you the days a real informer would have used, and at the end you have something the shortcut never gives: a decision made on evidence instead of terror. Sometimes it clears him. Sometimes it hangs him with his own logistics. Either way the column watched the leadership refuse to guess with a life, and that is worth more than the doubt it cost.

@ajust_proteger
go-to: post_event
on-arrival: paranoia += 4; disciplina += 3; unity += 2; leyenda += 1

You stand between the column and the compañero and say the sentence the armed struggle almost never manages: *we do not shoot our own on suspicion.* It is the principled choice and it is not the safe one — the doubt does not vanish, it just goes underground with the man it named, and if he was the ear, the Colonel's map keeps filling and the next losses are on your account. But the column saw the leadership refuse to become the enemy's instrument, and something holds in the movement's soul that the shooting would have broken. You have chosen to risk being betrayed over being certain to betray. History, on this one, tends to be kind to the choice and cruel to some of the people who made it.

@la_escision_armada
title: La escisión
