= La escisión

The argument the leadership has been holding shut blows open, and this being an armed movement, it does not blow open into a debate — it blows open into two commands. A bloc of columns, convinced the line is wrong (too militarist, too cautious, too centralized, too soft — the adjective varies, the rupture does not), announces it is going its own way: same enemy, same sierra, separate structure, and the terrible new arithmetic where two guerrillas that will not coordinate can be hunted one at a time. This is how the armed left of a whole continent turned a movement into a phone book of initials.

- @escision_dejar: Let them go cleanly. Draw the lines, divide the safe houses, agree not to fight each other, and grieve the strength you just halved.
- @escision_retener: Spend everything to hold them — concessions, a congress, the line bent toward theirs — and keep one army even if it is a compromised one.
- @escision_purgar: Treat the split as treason. Move against the leavers before they consolidate — the darkest road, and the one that ends with guerrillas killing guerrillas.

@escision_dejar
go-to: post_event
on-arrival: escisiones_armadas += 1; pres_valle -= 4; pres_jalisco -= 3; members -= 1; disciplina += 6; moral_columnas -= 3

You do the mature, mournful thing: a clean divorce. The safe houses divided without gunfire, a gentleman's agreement not to poach or betray, two movements where there was one — smaller, both of them, and each now carrying the specific loneliness of having been right at the cost of being fewer. Your columns are more coherent for having shed the disagreement, and weaker for having shed the people. Somewhere the other guerrilla issues its founding communiqué, and the DFS files it with satisfaction: they did not have to do this one themselves.

@escision_retener
go-to: post_event
choose-if: political_capital >= 5
unavailable-subtitle: Holding a splitting army together takes authority to spend, and the treasury of trust is empty.
on-arrival: political_capital -= 5; linea_guerra += 4; disciplina += 3; unity -= 2; moral_columnas += 2

You bend the line toward the leavers and pay for unity in the coin of coherence: a congress convened at gunpoint's remove, concessions that move the whole movement's strategy toward the faction that threatened to leave, the center giving ground to hold the edges. It works — one army walks out the door it nearly split through — and it is not free: the tail has learned it can move the dog by threatening to leave, and it will remember. You kept the numbers. You spent some of the thing that made them worth keeping.

@escision_purgar
go-to: post_event
on-arrival: escisiones_armadas += 1; ajusticiamientos += 1; paranoia += 12; disciplina -= 8; moral_columnas -= 10; memorial += 2; sup_students -= 4; leyenda -= 2

You call the split what the hardest voices insist it is — desertion, treason, an objective service to the enemy — and you move on the leavers before they can consolidate. It is the road with no bottom. Guerrillas hunting guerrillas, the two structures bleeding each other in the same sierra while the army watches from the ridgeline and takes notes, safe houses given up out of spite, the movement's own dead now including the ones it killed itself. Whatever the state does after this, it will not need to do much. You have shown it the shortest way to end a guerrilla, which is to convince it to end itself.
